# `?.` safe member access: `present` must be the looked-up value, `missing`
# must be nil. The `OM ` prefixes exist so CTest can assert on the VALUES --
# the engine's builtin-call echo prints the dict literal, so a bare
# `inimerse` in the combined output matched even while the lookup was broken
# (compiler.c passed a non-NUL-terminated StringView as the key, making the
# key the member name plus the whole rest of the source file).
obj = {"name": "inimerse"}
present = obj?.name
missing = nil?.name
say "OM present=" + present
say "OM missing=" + missing
